/E (LOOK WITH NEW EYES. A gardener's very first tool is not a shovel, it is a pair of careful eyes. When you slow down and really look, one plant becomes a hundred small wonders: tiny hairs, little veins, colors hiding inside colors. God packed the garden with beauty so you could look every day and still find something new. This unit we are learning to wonder, and wonder begins the moment you truly look.)
/Pg 15 0 R
/K [8]
>>
